If ever there was a city with a story to tell, it's Bristol. Enveloped in the hills of South West England, Bristol has developed an inimitable identity and fiercely independent spirit, crafted by its passionate locals.

From the iconic [Clifton Suspension Bridge](https://cliftonbridge.org.uk/visit-explore/) spanning the [Avon Gorge](https://visitbristol.co.uk/blog/post/natural-wonders-near-bristol/) to the bustling [Harbourside](https://visitbristol.co.uk/discover/areas/harbourside/), the elegant Georgian streets of [Clifton](https://visitbristol.co.uk/discover/areas/clifton/) and the historic [Old City](https://visitbristol.co.uk/discover/areas/city-centre-and-old-city/), there is plenty to explore. Bristol is famous for its [street art](https://visitbristol.co.uk/things-to-do/street-art/), with Banksy's work found across the city, and for a thriving independent [food](https://visitbristol.co.uk/food-and-drink/), music and arts scene. Every summer the skies fill with colour during the [Bristol International Balloon Fiesta](https://visitbristol.co.uk/event/bristol-international-balloon-fiesta/198734301/), and the Harbourside comes alive for the [Bristol Harbour Festival](https://visitbristol.co.uk/event/bristol-harbour-festival/236925301/).

Find out more about what to see and do at [Visit Bristol](https://visitbristol.co.uk/).

<figure class="my-8">
  <enhanced:img
